From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:19:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] combase: Export the apartment's IRundown when its context is
 created.

IContextCallback::ContextCallback from another apartment reaches the target apartment through
the IRundown object at IPID {ffffffff-ffff-ffff-<oxid>}, which is exported only with the first
object the apartment marshals. An apartment that never marshaled anything made the call fail,
and C++/WinRT programs that co_await on a background thread and resume in their STA through
ContextCallback (the Windows App SDK file picker in Minecraft Bedrock) crashed. Start remoting
when the context token is first created, on the apartment's own thread.

Original work for macrock (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

Topic: com-context
---
 dlls/combase/combase.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/combase/combase.c b/dlls/combase/combase.c
index 94e256f7cc1771a6a29e2f3e6399e05ebbdf5511..1418689faaeafabba926e5f73370b3038a218236 100644
--- a/dlls/combase/combase.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/combase.c
@@ -2856,6 +2856,9 @@ HRESULT WINAPI CoGetContextToken(ULONG_PTR *token)
         context->reported_ref = 0;
         context->oxid = apt->oxid;
 
+        /* Export the apartment's IRundown, which other apartments' ContextCallback calls need. */
+        rpc_start_remoting(apt);
+
         if (apt->multi_threaded)
         {
             EnterCriticalSection(&context_cs);
